The restricted static PyTorch data decoder is adapted from this repository's
Sezika.IndependentModelTool PickleReader. It interprets data descriptors only;
no pickle global, callback, Python code, or arbitrary object is executed.

Model weights, tokenizer assets and their provenance/licensing remain separate.
No model assets are embedded in this project or its program image.

The separate Laya adapter ports Laya 0.3.20 behavior with source revision
4066d5d5fbf08b66c6757ddeedbd797bd7655bc0. Its source-lock SHA256 is
901527bdd7da7732c2d12903a45dcc1984ac2187e14214ae780286c585f2e287;
the common/agent source identities are recorded separately in Laya/PortProof.cs.
The 46 input and 42 decoder checks consume historical inputs and logits and
do not execute the upstream implementation or verify a complete neural forward.

The tokenizer asset and the 267-item regression golden retain their separate
provenance and license records. The golden in
tests/fixtures/tokenizer-mmbert-boundaries.v1.json records tokenizers 0.22.2
and original minimal Apache-2.0 regression text. This declaration concerns
that fixture, not the license or approval of model or tokenizer assets.
The three Transformers source declarations above do not replace these
separate adapter, asset and fixture records. No upstream tokenizer is executed.
